<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Front (Czechoslovakia)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1945">1945</a>–<a href="/years/1990">1990</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National Front was the coalition of parties that governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> from 1945 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosice-programme">Košice Programme</a>. After the Communist takeover of February 1948 it became an umbrella through which the Communist Party controlled all permitted parties and mass organisations. It lost its role after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/velvet-revolution">Velvet Revolution</a> of 1989 and was dissolved in 1990.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/national-front-czechoslovakia.jpg" alt="National Front (Czechoslovakia)" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ThecentreCZ · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_the_National_Front_of_Czechs_and_Slovaks.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
